  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 133 AM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nThursday night through Tuesday\nAssessment...a certainty of very windy conditions late Thursday\nnight and Friday with frost Friday night. The probability of a\nfreeze is at 20-30 percent.\n\nA strong cold front will sweep through the area Thursday night \nbringing very windy conditions to the area late Thursday night \nthrough mid-day Friday. All models show a trop fold moving through \nthe area during this time frame which will increase winds. The \nmodels generally agree the trop fold will be down to 400-500 mb but \nsome solutions have the trop fold as sub 500 mb.\n\nRegardless of the solution, there is a potential for wind headlines. \nCurrently that probability is at 20-30 percent.\n\nCold Canadian high pressure brings a near certainty of frost to the \narea Friday night into Saturday morning. Cloud cover will be the key \nto how cold it will get. The potential for freezing temperatures is \nalso there, especially north of Highway 30. Right now the \nprobability of freezing temperatures is at 20-30 percent.",
